shape: Tapered Directional/Directional
flex pattern: Directional Flex (increases pop in tail, stiffer nose)
camber type: Directional Camber (rocker in nose, traditional camber retained)
width: Standard
inserts: The Channel (Burton Channel mounting system, compatible with most major binding brands, works best with Burton EST bindings)
laminate: 45° Carbon Highlights (tip to tail carbon layer with 45° angled fibres)
core: Dragonfly 600G Core with Multizone EGD and Squeezebox
core technology - Multizone EGD: Aligns wood grain along heel and toe edge in four separate zones adjacent to the channel
core technology - Squeezebox: Thicker powerful sections combined with thinner flexible sections profiled throughout the core
base: Sintered WFO (extra absorbent, high density sintered material infused with specially formulated wax)
balanced freeride geometry: Setback camber and stance-centred sidecut (feels like a twin when flat based, tight turns and effortless float when directional)
infinite ride: Boards overbuilt in factory then broken down by machinery for consistent performance over time
resin: Super Sap Epoxy (bio-based resin, reduces carbon footprint by 50% over petroleum-based epoxies)
designed for: Steep and deep Japanese mountain terrain, tree riding, powder
